  "notes": "Transitive verb. The subject that blocks is often an abstract concept (weather, lack of resources, opposition) rather than a person.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {行|ゆ}く{手|て}を{阻|はば}む (to block one's path)\n- {進出|しんしゅつ}を{阻|はば}む (to block an advance)\n- {成長|せいちょう}を{阻|はば}む (to hinder growth)\n- {勝利|しょうり}を{阻|はば}む (to prevent a victory)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{妨|さまた}げる is a close synonym but sounds slightly more literary and is more often used with human agents. {阻|はば}む emphasizes the idea of standing as a barrier, while {妨|さまた}げる focuses on the act of interfering.",
